window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/resources/security-v27-092-9e023a2540780afc.json"]={sha256:"9e023a2540780afcda74302c2f1f2403cc4a14314da57bb1f754bafdf7a20f03",value:{"sources":[{"id":"v27-case-237b1f08ae2de38b","url":"https://sre.google/sre-book/handling-overload/","title":"Google SRE Book: handling overload","titleEn":"Google SRE Book: handling overload","publisher":"Google","scope":"查證具名案例與原理背景。課內數值、故障資料與判準為原創教學假設；請勿當作廠商規格或操作程序。","scopeEn":"Establish named case and principle context. Numbers, fault data, and criteria are original teaching assumptions, not manufacturer specifications or operating procedures."}],"media":{"courses":[{"courseId":"security-v27-092","videos":[],"guides":[]}]},"related":{"courses":[{"courseId":"security-v27-092","related":[{"id":"security-v27-093","referenceUrls":["https://sre.google/sre-book/addressing-cascading-failures/"],"title":"Google SRE：共同相依與最小失效割集","titleEn":"Google SRE: shared dependencies and minimal failure cut sets","why":"用兩課的可觀察驗收條件比較模型邊界：交付call-tree.json、attempt-ledger.csv、retry-policy.md與amplification-report.json，含root_id及每個parent_attempt_id。","whyEn":"Compare model boundaries using observable acceptance criteria: Deliver call-tree.json, attempt-ledger.csv, retry-policy.md and amplification-report.json, including root_id and parent_attempt_id for every node so another apprentice can reconstruct the fan-out independently.","difference":"將服務條件寫為D AND (Z1 OR Z2)，列出使服務失效的最小元件集合，並逐一測試單元件故障。","differenceEn":"Express service availability as D AND (Z1 OR Z2), enumerate minimal component sets that make it false, and test every single-component failure using explicit Boolean fixtures.","transfer":"保留單位與邊界條件，僅轉移可證明相容的驗證方法。","transferEn":"Retain units and boundary conditions; transfer only demonstrably compatible verification methods.","practice":["SRE過載處理討論分層重試放大及預算；本例假設每次都失敗、同步串列且沒有快取，計算最壞嘗試次數而非預期成功率。 本課所有數值、事件與系統狀態均為原創合成資料；只在本機檔案與授權隔離練習中處理，不接觸生產設備或他人資料。 三個重試層A,B,C，每層一次上游呼叫最多發出3個下游attempt。單一root_id貫穿所有合成記錄，attempt_id不可重用。 多層重試最底層3×3×3=27次；僅C最多三次、A/B各一次，最底層只有3次，降低24次。","SRE討論共同相依與連鎖失效；本課只做邏輯失效枚舉，不假設故障互相獨立，也不把情境通過比例當成實際SLA。 本課所有數值、事件與系統狀態均為原創合成資料；只在本機檔案與授權隔離練習中處理，不接觸生產設備或他人資料。 D代表共用解析、Z1與Z2代表兩區；三個單點故障情境分別只關閉D、Z1、Z2，其餘皆正常。 失D即失效，單失Z1或Z2仍可用，通過2/3=66.666667%；最小割集為{D}與{Z1,Z2}。","比較兩個模型的輸入、誤差與驗收條件，記錄不能沿用的假設。"],"practiceEn":["SRE overload guidance addresses layered retry amplification and budgets. This fixture assumes every attempt fails, execution is synchronous and serial, and no cache intervenes; it counts worst-case attempts, not expected success probability. Every quantity, event and system state below is original synthetic teaching data. Work only on local files or an explicitly authorized isolated lab, without production access or other people’s data. Retry layers A, B and C each issue at most three downstream attempts for one upstream call. A single root_id links the synthetic trace, while every attempt_id remains distinct. Layered retries generate 3×3×3=27 leaf attempts. With only C allowed three attempts and A/B each allowed one, the leaf receives three attempts, a reduction of twenty-four.","SRE discusses shared dependencies and cascading failure. This exercise enumerates logical failure scenarios without assuming independent probabilities or interpreting the fraction of passing scenarios as a real service-level guarantee. Every quantity, event and system state below is original synthetic teaching data. Work only on local files or an explicitly authorized isolated lab, without production access or other people’s data. D is the shared resolver and Z1/Z2 are regions. Three single-failure scenarios independently disable D, Z1 or Z2 while all other components remain available. D failure disables the service, while either individual region failure is tolerated, passing 2/3=66.666667%. Minimal cut sets are {D} and {Z1,Z2}.","Compare inputs, errors, and criteria; document assumptions that cannot be transferred."]},{"id":"security-v27-002","referenceUrls":["https://spiffe.io/docs/latest/spire-about/spire-concepts/"],"title":"SPIRE 註冊：選擇器交集與身分誤授風險","titleEn":"SPIRE registration: selector intersections and unintended identity grants","why":"用兩課的可觀察驗收條件比較模型邊界：交付call-tree.json、attempt-ledger.csv、retry-policy.md與amplification-report.json，含root_id及每個parent_attempt_id。","whyEn":"Compare model boundaries using observable acceptance criteria: Deliver call-tree.json, attempt-ledger.csv, retry-policy.md and amplification-report.json, including root_id and parent_attempt_id for every node so another apprentice can reconstruct the fan-out independently.","difference":"建立12筆合成程序記錄，分別含節點、namespace、service account及映像摘要；先固定parent身分，再畫出三項工作負載選擇器的交集。","differenceEn":"Create 12 synthetic process records containing node, namespace, service account and image digest. Hold the parent identity fixed, then draw the intersection of three workload-selector sets.","transfer":"保留單位與邊界條件，僅轉移可證明相容的驗證方法。","transferEn":"Retain units and boundary conditions; transfer only demonstrably compatible verification methods.","practice":["SRE過載處理討論分層重試放大及預算；本例假設每次都失敗、同步串列且沒有快取，計算最壞嘗試次數而非預期成功率。 本課所有數值、事件與系統狀態均為原創合成資料；只在本機檔案與授權隔離練習中處理，不接觸生產設備或他人資料。 三個重試層A,B,C，每層一次上游呼叫最多發出3個下游attempt。單一root_id貫穿所有合成記錄，attempt_id不可重用。 多層重試最底層3×3×3=27次；僅C最多三次、A/B各一次，最底層只有3次，降低24次。","選擇器必須共同成立；重複觀測同一程序不能增加可授權程序數。用明列的集合交集對照註冊條目，並將節點認證與工作負載認證分層。 namespace與service account共同符合的程序有8筆，其中5筆映像摘要也符合；變更摘要白名單後另有2筆符合，母體仍12筆。 初始可授權比例5/12×100=41.6666667%；修訂後7/12×100=58.3333333%，其餘不得因同節點就取得此身分。","比較兩個模型的輸入、誤差與驗收條件，記錄不能沿用的假設。"],"practiceEn":["SRE overload guidance addresses layered retry amplification and budgets. This fixture assumes every attempt fails, execution is synchronous and serial, and no cache intervenes; it counts worst-case attempts, not expected success probability. Every quantity, event and system state below is original synthetic teaching data. Work only on local files or an explicitly authorized isolated lab, without production access or other people’s data. Retry layers A, B and C each issue at most three downstream attempts for one upstream call. A single root_id links the synthetic trace, while every attempt_id remains distinct. Layered retries generate 3×3×3=27 leaf attempts. With only C allowed three attempts and A/B each allowed one, the leaf receives three attempts, a reduction of twenty-four.","Required selectors must hold together; observing a process twice does not create another eligible process. Compare explicit set intersections with registration entries while separating node attestation from workload attestation. Eight processes jointly match namespace and service account; five also match the image digest. An approved digest-list revision admits two more of those eight, while the population remains 12. Eligible share is 5/12×100=41.6666667%; the revision yields 7/12×100=58.3333333%. Remaining processes must not receive the identity merely because they share a node.","Compare inputs, errors, and criteria; document assumptions that cannot be transferred."]}],"references":[{"id":"v27-case-5d487fe40fc84b48","url":"https://sre.google/sre-book/addressing-cascading-failures/","title":"Google SRE Book: addressing cascading failures","titleEn":"Google SRE Book: addressing cascading failures","publisher":"Google","scope":"查證具名案例與原理背景。課內數值、故障資料與判準為原創教學假設；請勿當作廠商規格或操作程序。","scopeEn":"Establish named case and principle context. Numbers, fault data, and criteria are original teaching assumptions, not manufacturer specifications or operating procedures."},{"id":"v27-case-3c67d91571cd08ae","url":"https://spiffe.io/docs/latest/spire-about/spire-concepts/","title":"SPIRE Concepts and workload registration","titleEn":"SPIRE Concepts and workload registration","publisher":"SPIFFE","scope":"查證具名案例與原理背景。課內數值、故障資料與判準為原創教學假設；請勿當作廠商規格或操作程序。","scopeEn":"Establish named case and principle context. Numbers, fault data, and criteria are original teaching assumptions, not manufacturer specifications or operating procedures."}],"overview":"比較相鄰案例與另一組案例的模型、可量測結果及可轉移的驗證方法。","overviewEn":"Compare neighboring and cross-group cases by model, measurable outcome, and transferable verification method."}]},"places":{"courses":[]},"vendors":{"courses":[],"vendors":[]}}};
